WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.271
-Everything all set?

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.240
Yeah. No, I'm --

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.376
I'm excited, too.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.379
I hope I'm not jinxing it.
Oh, hey.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:18.217
I don't ask a ton of you guys,

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:22.088
but I'd like to make
a quick request.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.389
Can you all...

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:28.394
take the wax out of your ears
for a second?

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:31.131
It's a [bleep] Negroni.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:43.209
Somebody said, uh,
"Houdini wasn't a magician,

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.278
he was an illusionist."

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:48.714
Magic isn't real.

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:50.683
Well, maybe you should give
that correction

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.251
to this dove.

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:54.187
[ Poof sound ]

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:56.956
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.500
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.903
[ Scattered applause ]

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.808
"Everything's all set."

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:22.948
Find the dove.

00:01:22.948 --> 00:01:24.818
It's got to be somewhere.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:39.566
Bane, I was told Bane was never
imprisoned in Arkham Asylum.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:42.902
If that was an effort to get me
to do my Bane, try harder.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:51.945
I said Tele-mun-do,
it's Tele-moon-do.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:57.617
Obviously,
I'm hesitant to say "moon"

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:00.220
lest I summon this guy.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:09.595
This was sent in from a jackal.
A jackal made this.

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.965
I'm assuming in their basement

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:15.034
while their victims
were forced to watch.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.674
I feel like if this guy
could talk, he'd say --

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.577
[ Imitating Bane ]
"As I terrorize Gotham...

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:33.353
I will feed its people hope
to poison their soul.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.822
Hope and chicken McNuggets."

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:46.365
We said Trump's civil trial
could decimate his fortune.

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:53.806
A lot of you said "decimate"
means to reduce by 10%,

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.107
and of course, that makes sense.

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:57.777
"Deci" means "10."
"Mate" means "reduce."

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:01.047
I don't know,
I didn't do that part.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.849
But I did look it up,
and there's truth to it.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:06.785
So, in the military
of ancient Rome,

00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:09.622
"decimation" was a form
of military discipline

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:12.525
in which every 10th man
in a group

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:15.962
was executed
by members of his cohort.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:19.765
This discipline was used
to punish large groups

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:23.168
guilty of capital offenses
such as cowardice, mutiny,

00:03:23.168 --> 00:03:24.670
and desertions.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.807
I can imagine the hardest part,

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:31.744
is picking the one, you know?

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.078
Because, I mean,
we have ten writers.

00:03:33.078 --> 00:03:34.113
I don't know how we could
ever...

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.548
Oh, Reiss.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.550
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:44.157
Speaking of writers,
I showed this headshot

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:47.459
of Matt Goldich,
his new headshot.

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:49.428
I complimented how cool
he looked.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:50.763
One of you said "Cool?

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.164
It looks like he went
to the barber and said,

00:03:52.164 --> 00:03:54.200
'Give me the Richard Lewis.'"

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:04.410
People are obsessed

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:08.914
with the way I hold and operate
my pencil during "Corrections."

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:12.885
People think I tap it
too much on the desk.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:16.555
Someone said, "Is your desk
covered with pencil marks?"

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.057
Of course not.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:20.560
We switch out
the desk every week.

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:24.463
Which is probably why NBC

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:26.699
is always harping on us
about the budget.

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:33.238
Also, a lot of you thought
I almost poked my eye out

00:04:33.238 --> 00:04:35.375
last "Corrections"
with the way I wildly

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.109
gesticulated with my pencil.

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:38.344
Let's take a look.

00:04:39.611 --> 00:04:41.580
I also, we had a great --

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.516
I know what I'm doing.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:47.720
I've been using a pencil
for a long time.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.889
I've got nothing
to worry about.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.591
Hey, there was a real
lack of lightness

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.726
to your comments this week.

00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:58.530
This one was nice.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:01.166
"Don't think it's there yet,
but Seth's Australian accent

00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:02.501
was definitely better
this week."

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:03.535
Only problem?

00:05:03.535 --> 00:05:06.005
Last week,
I did a Scottish accent.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:11.678
Here's one that took me
awhile to unpack.

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:16.282
"Can we please get somebody
else? I hardly watch anymore."

00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:25.224
Somebody else to do this?

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:30.163
You want somebody else
to do "Corrections"?

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:39.205
Someone wrote, "The amount
that Seth jokes about

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:41.274
how little his wife cares
for his career interests

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:45.144
or his feelings in general
makes me wonder

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:48.214
if it's actually a joke.
Are you guys okay?"

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:51.184
I mean, I think we're fine.

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:56.656
I mean, the way you said it

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:59.125
certainly didn't
make things sound great.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:03.295
But, honey,
if you're watching --

00:06:03.295 --> 00:06:05.664
No?

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:07.633
She told you?

00:06:12.604 --> 00:06:15.975
Had a Rick Roll last week.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:22.048
Got a lot of feedback
on the Rick Roll.

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:25.284
My favorite was
a back-and-forth --

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.153
because that's the great thing
about sometimes

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:30.422
you can really unfold
the jackal comments.

00:06:30.422 --> 00:06:33.159
And I like when you
all talk to one another,

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:37.596
because it means you're not
talking to other people.

00:06:37.596 --> 00:06:39.231
Someone wrote, "If
you're going to Rick Roll,

00:06:39.231 --> 00:06:42.535
at least play the whole song."

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:46.004
Then someone wrote,
"The whole song?

00:06:46.004 --> 00:06:49.007
That's not how
Rick Rolling works."

00:06:49.007 --> 00:06:51.811
And someone said, "I don't care.
I like that song."

00:06:55.614 --> 00:06:57.049
Well, to that person,
I just say,

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.484
you know how you're using
the internet

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:01.019
to watch this right now?

00:07:01.019 --> 00:07:03.589
You can use it for other stuff.

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:08.060
It's not just for "Corrections."

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:13.766
Someone wrote,
"Rick Rolling in 2023?

00:07:13.766 --> 00:07:15.401
Okay, boomer."

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.340
So now I'm a boomer?

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.776
I mean, I guess.

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:27.480
I do boomer things.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.282
Like getting [bleep] trashed
with Dua Lipa

00:07:30.282 --> 00:07:31.884
on a Friday afternoon?

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:39.192
Go to bed, kids.
The adults are talking.

00:07:45.931 --> 00:07:51.737
But I saved the most --
the harshest for last.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.339
"Rick Rolling and Meyers
are the same,

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:57.843
having been funny since 2010."

00:07:57.843 --> 00:08:01.213
That's very hurtful.

00:08:01.213 --> 00:08:07.553
But your words are not
going to change who I am.

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.989
No matter what you say to me,

00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:11.190
I am never...

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.725
-♪ Gonna give you up ♪

00:08:12.725 --> 00:08:15.495
♪ Never gonna let you down ♪

00:08:23.268 --> 00:08:24.770
-The jack-in-the-box last week,

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:28.274
I found out it was made by
Beez McKeever,

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:30.743
who created props,
made props for

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:33.045
"Mystery Science Theater 3000,"
which is a fantastic show.

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:37.483
How about that?
That's just a cool fact.

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:41.687
Giant pandas and red pandas
aren't related.

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:43.222
This is a fact
the giant panda reminds

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:46.559
the red panda of every day.

00:08:46.559 --> 00:08:50.229
It's where we got the expression
"red-headed step-panda."

00:08:54.099 --> 00:08:55.701
Someone else wrote,
"The word panda"

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.236
originally meant the red panda,

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:59.138
but after the bear
was discovered,

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:01.006
it was named the Giant Panda,

00:09:01.006 --> 00:09:03.242
and the original was called
the Lesser Panda."

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:06.746
Which was later changed
to the Fewer Panda.

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:13.252
This has been "Animal Flubs."

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:14.420
-♪ Animal Flubs ♪

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.488
♪ Animal Flubs ♪

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:17.623
-You're adopted...

00:09:17.623 --> 00:09:19.091
bitch.

00:09:21.827 --> 00:09:24.630
-Oh, no.

00:09:29.301 --> 00:09:32.604
-Oh!

00:09:32.604 --> 00:09:34.974
Oh, no!

00:09:36.642 --> 00:09:39.478
[ Laughter ]

00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:54.059
And you're like, "Oh, you should
rehearse 'Corrections.'"

00:09:54.059 --> 00:09:55.394
No.

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:58.263
[ Eyeball bouncing ]

00:09:58.263 --> 00:10:01.333
You guys, pretty cool, this is
a true story, great thing,

00:10:01.333 --> 00:10:04.670
my crew last week after
"Corrections" surprised me.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.806
I went back to my dressing room,
walked out of my dressing room,

00:10:06.806 --> 00:10:08.708
surprised me with
a 50th birthday party.

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:10.175
Totally caught me off-guard.

00:10:10.175 --> 00:10:13.079
In my defense, it was a full
three weeks before my birthday.

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:18.650
It's a little bit like
somebody in February

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:20.419
going, "April Fools!

00:10:20.419 --> 00:10:22.287
You should see your face."

00:10:22.287 --> 00:10:24.924
You're like, alright.

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:26.058
They're like,
"Were you surprised?"

00:10:26.058 --> 00:10:28.260
I'm like,
"Of [bleep] course I was."

00:10:34.566 --> 00:10:36.268
But it genuinely
meant the world to me.

00:10:36.268 --> 00:10:37.837
And it was the best.
It was the best.

00:10:37.837 --> 00:10:41.907
Because, you know, one of
the things about any party

00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:44.610
I have for my birthday,
I hardly have ever had any.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:46.178
I have, uh --

00:10:46.178 --> 00:10:50.316
my birthday is December 28th,
which is, I think,

00:10:50.316 --> 00:10:52.718
affectionately known
as the holiday taint.

00:10:56.822 --> 00:10:58.924
It's very rare for people
to get together,

00:10:58.924 --> 00:11:01.793
so I appreciated that they
slid up the calendar and did it.

00:11:01.793 --> 00:11:03.462
I got some presents.

00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:08.534
Best present
was from Kenny Coyle.

00:11:11.169 --> 00:11:13.673
Can't tell you what it is.

00:11:15.775 --> 00:11:20.413
But I can tell you you spell
Coyle "NSFW."

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.755
I did get some some
Christmas gifts.

00:11:29.755 --> 00:11:33.125
I'm a Steeler fan.

00:11:33.125 --> 00:11:35.060
People know I'm a Steeler fan.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:37.396
Christmas is coming up.

00:11:37.396 --> 00:11:40.332
Someone sent this.

00:11:40.332 --> 00:11:42.802
Very nice.

00:11:42.802 --> 00:11:45.404
And then I would say that
is as nice as this is...

00:11:45.404 --> 00:11:48.040
not.

00:11:53.812 --> 00:11:56.448
"The Steelers
have won the toss...

00:11:56.448 --> 00:11:59.752
and elected to kill."

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:04.990
-Oh, look at this.

00:12:07.826 --> 00:12:09.528
Surprise present.

00:12:09.528 --> 00:12:13.733
I guess the
birthday surprise continues.

00:12:26.578 --> 00:12:28.013
-Look at that.

00:12:28.013 --> 00:12:30.015
It's a one-winged dove.

00:12:32.251 --> 00:12:34.754
Stevie Nicks week.

